<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Entity>
  <!--
    NEW TABLE — WBS 6.9, Trustee Portal Visual Refresh / Round-Statistics Landing Screen
    (TAD docs/architecture/trustee-portal-visual-refresh-architecture.md, ADR-028, section
    3.5). Serves FR-057 (which round the landing screen shows), FR-058's "date the round
    opened" and FR-063 (finance figures). Hand-maintained, Tier 2, non-personal — the round's
    calendar and financial position, entered by hand. Read DIRECTLY by the trustee (TAD
    section 5.4 step 1); this is not a Round entity and scopes no application visibility
    (TAD section 3.5: "This is not a Round entity, and it must not be read as one").

    SHAPE COPIED FROM rev_setting/Entity.xml, NOT GUESSED: OrganizationOwned, the D-018
    FormXml/SavedQueries empty-marker fix (see rev_setting's own file for the full
    rationale — without them this entity's FormXml/ and SavedQueries/ folders drop silently
    at pack time, IMP-0006), and an alternate key on the round name for the same
    "cannot be entered twice" reason rev_setting's key exists.

    OQ-036 ANSWERED (ADR-028): the reviewer offered two mechanisms — extend an existing
    finance-accessible table (rev_bankaccount / rev_payment), or a new table Finance fills
    in. The first is rejected on evidence: both finance tables are Tier 4 with every
    securable column inside REV_FinanceOnly, and the REV Trustee role holds no table
    privilege on either — extending either would put a non-personal charity-level figure
    behind a Tier 4 personal-financial control, unreadable by its only audience, on a row
    whose retention clock belongs to a Grant. This table is the second option.

    Decimal, never Money, for every measure (C-TECH-070 clause 2, IMP-0047): a Money
    column's automatic _base twin cannot be secured, and this single-currency organisation
    gains nothing from Money. Nothing here needs securing, but the precedent set elsewhere
    in this solution is not diverged from without reason.

    No column secured — these are charity-level aggregate figures with no data subject
    (SDD section 7.2's own row for this record: "Not personal data — aggregate charity-
    level figures... no applicant identity"). No relationship to rev_application or to
    anything else (TAD section 3.6): this table does not participate in the
    Applicant/Application cascade spine and grants no access.

    rev_roundopenedon is ENTERED, not derived from MIN(rev_submittedon) — a round with a
    quiet first week would report a later open date and an inflated applications-per-day
    figure. FR-058's own words are "the date the round opened", a calendar fact the charity
    owns (TAD section 3.5).

    A-R25 (accepted, TAD section 11): the REV Finance role does not exist in solution
    source yet (Roles/ holds only REV Admin, REV Service Automation, REV Trustee), so
    REV Admin is the interim maintainer of this table's Create/Read/Write grant — see
    Roles/REV Admin/REV Admin.xml. The grant to REV Finance is specified in the TAD and
    applies automatically once that role is built; nothing here blocks on it.
  -->
  <Name LocalizedName="Round Finance" OriginalName="Round Finance">rev_roundfinance</Name>
  <EntityInfo>
    <entity Name="rev_roundfinance">
      <LocalizedNames>
        <LocalizedName description="Round Finance" languagecode="1033" />
      </LocalizedNames>
      <LocalizedCollectionNames>
        <LocalizedCollectionName description="Round Finances" languagecode="1033" />
      </LocalizedCollectionNames>
      <Descriptions>
        <Description description="One row per review round: the round's open/close calendar and its charity-level finance figures, entered by hand (TAD section 3.5, ADR-028). Not personal data. Read directly by the trustee portal's landing screen (FR-057, FR-058's open date, FR-063)." languagecode="1033" />
      </Descriptions>
      <attributes>
