          <DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
          <IsAuditEnabled>1</IsAuditEnabled>
          <IsSecured>0</IsSecured>
          <displaynames>
            <displayname description="Is Open" languagecode="1033" />
          </displaynames>
          <Descriptions>
            <Description description="Which round the landing screen shows (FR-057). Read with $filter=rev_isopen eq true, top 2 (TAD section 5.4) — exactly one open round is an invariant asserted in code, not assumed; zero or two rows both render a diagnostic state rather than a guess. DefaultValue=0: a new round row does not silently become the shown round." languagecode="1033" />
          </Descriptions>
        </attribute>
        <attribute PhysicalName="rev_roundopenedon">
          <Type>datetime</Type>
          <Name>rev_roundopenedon</Name>
          <LogicalName>rev_roundopenedon</LogicalName>
          <RequiredLevel>None</RequiredLevel>
          <Format>date</Format>
          <DateTimeBehavior>DateOnly</DateTimeBehavior>
          <IsAuditEnabled>1</IsAuditEnabled>
          <IsSecured>0</IsSecured>
          <displaynames>
            <displayname description="Round Opened On" languagecode="1033" />
          </displaynames>
          <Descriptions>
            <Description description="FR-058's 'the date the round opened'. Entered, not derived from MIN(applications received) — a round with a quiet first week would otherwise report a later open date and an inflated applications-per-day figure (TAD section 3.5). An administrative fact the charity owns." languagecode="1033" />
